      "description": "The (Vowel + Consonant)உயிர்மெய் எழுத்துக்கள் are compound letters in Tamil formed by combining a consonant (மெய்) with a vowel (உயிர்). For example, the consonant ஞ் (N) combines with vowels to form ஞ, ஞா, ஞி, ஞீ, ஞு, ஞூ, ஞெ, ஞே, ஞை, ஞொ, ஞோ, and ஞௌ. "
